                            P·R·E·S·E·N·T·S

                >>  Dynamite V1.5 by Modem Boy/oTL!  <<
                       Asl.Library V38+ Required.

Introduction:
~~~~~~~~~~~~~
Dynamite  is  a  fast and small (3704 bytes) LhA Checker-Stripper-Adder
written in Amiga_E!!!

There is no big differences from other checkers, but Dynamite is one of
the fastest (or the faster???) around, so use it and have fun!


Bug Fixed:
~~~~~~~~~~
Now  you  can  process  a file in "Ram Disk:" or in any other directory
that haves one or more spaces in its name.


Options:
~~~~~~~~
There is a '-r' option that allows you to open a file-requester, useful
for CLI usage!  Asl.Library V38+ is needed.


Ami-Express Usage:
~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~
Make  sure  that the files Dynamite.Strip & Dynamite.Add are in your s:
directory  (otherwise  Dynamite  will  perform  only  an integrity test
without  stripping  or  adding  anything!), then edit 'em with a normal
text editor.

LhA  must  be  in your c:  directory (of coz!), or make it resident for
maximum speed and low memory usage (on multinodes systems).

      Usage: resident c:LhA pure


The file "bbs:fcheck/lha.info" must have the following tool-types:

------------------->cut here<--------------------
CHECKER=C:DYNAMITE
ERROR.1=WARNING: Skipping corrupt/extraneous data
ERROR.2=Operation not entirely successful
ERROR.3=Failed
------------------->cut here<--------------------

Better using the lha.info included in this archive, so there will be no
chance of mistakes.


-------------------------------[ NOTE ]--------------------------------

Dynamite  may  be  used  from  CLI and with any other BBS program (like
CNet, Dialog...)!

      CLI Usage: Dynamite [<options>] <filename>

        Options:  -r = File-Requester (Multi-Selection is allowed!)

